  "behavior": "Private FlashInfer plan metadata permits retained prefill/decode graphs; full graph build counters remain unchanged for repeated requests at capacity 2 and increase again after forced eviction.",
  "limitations": [
    "Two timing processes per capacity, in ABBA order; each contributes two repeated requests. No statistical-significance claim.",
    "B1, short-context, teacher-forced diagnostic execution with full-vocabulary logits. The request timer includes oracle checking and drain. This is not HTTP latency, serving TPOT or throughput.",
    "Both timing arms use the same final binary with the ownership fix; they compare residency capacity 1 versus 2, not old versus new kernel performance.",
    "Initial request materialization and final forced eviction are excluded from the repeated-request medians, but all raw timings and counters are retained.",
    "Finite graph residency defaults to one and must be explicitly raised. All compiled buckets are conservatively budgeted; automatic residency selection from a joint budget remains open.",
    "The provider metadata charge is 8 MiB per prepared plan plus replacement peak; float scratch is 128 MiB shared. CUDA driver-internal graph/module memory is outside payload estimates. Process-exit memory observation does not prove a live-process memory peak.",
    "Single H20 and serialized execution on one owning stream. Long-context/ragged multi-request model transitions, cross-stream and multi-device ownership need separate qualification.",
    "The independent Transformers model oracle uses the local DeepGEMM math library. Metadata and reference files are fingerprinted; no new full-weight-payload hash or new schedule search was performed.",
    "The old provider regression has retained failing output and observed source files, but no frozen baseline binary receipt. It establishes metadata overwrite, not a fully reproduced historical build."
